From ecda60ed15f6d05dc2648bf28eb50e0bef800f73 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Teguh Sobirin <teguh@sobir.in>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 22:37:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: tolerate a missing hwmon device on thermal
 cleanup

A recovery that fails before the thermal devices are re-registered
leaves the cleanup to run again on the next crash, where
hwmon_device_unregister() would dereference the NULL left behind.

Signed-off-by: Teguh Sobirin <teguh@sobir.in>

Backport to Armada Linux 7.2.6; retain existing WCN7860 and QDSS support.
Source: https://github.com/RetroidPocket/linux/commit/ecda60ed15f6d05dc2648bf28eb50e0bef800f73
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/thermal.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/thermal.c
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/thermal.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/thermal.c
@@ -260,6 +260,10 @@
 	if (!ar)
 		return;
 
+	/* a failed recovery leaves this NULL for the next crash */
+	if (!ar->thermal.hwmon_dev)
+		return;
+
 	hwmon_device_unregister(ar->thermal.hwmon_dev);
 	ar->thermal.hwmon_dev = NULL;
 
